# Git workflow & localhost preview

**One local checkout = one branch in the browser.** `localhost:4321` serves whatever branch is checked out in this repo folder. The user controls preview via Cursor’s **Checkout branch** on a chat — not by agents switching to *unrelated* branches silently.

## New feature work → new branch off `main`

**Default for VCDwebsite (Cursor and Claude):** start feature / fix work on a **new branch based on latest `main`**. **Do not implement on `main`** unless Anto **explicitly** says to work on `main` for that task.

1. Before the first edit: `git fetch origin` (when network allows), then `git switch main && git pull` if needed so local `main` is current.
2. Create and check out the feature branch: `git switch -c feat/<short-name>` (or the name Anto gives).
3. Call `SetActiveBranch` so this chat’s UI tracks that branch.
4. Say which branch you’re on when it matters.

This *is* permission to create/switch to **that feature branch for this chat’s work**. Do **not** wait for Anto to say “make a branch” for ordinary new features — branch first, then edit.

## Do not steal the preview for unrelated work

- Do **not** switch this checkout to some other chat’s branch, or to an unrelated feature, without Anto asking (e.g. Checkout branch, or “check out …”).
- Before any git operation, run `git branch --show-current` and mention which branch you’re on if it matters.

## Parallel work (other chats / features)

- Prefer **cloud agents** for side features so commits push to GitHub without changing the user’s local checkout.
- Local alternative: **git worktree** in a sibling folder (e.g. `../VCDwebsite-<branch>`) — never steal the main repo checkout for parallel edits.
- Do **not** start unrelated feature work on the user’s current preview branch without asking.

## Commits

- Only stage and commit files changed **in this chat session**. Leave other unstaged edits alone.
- One logical change set per branch/PR. Say which branch commits land on.

### Content vs engine — never mix them in one commit

`src/content/**` and `public/images/**` are the **content surface**: Anto publishes those to `main` himself from the dev save bar ("Save & Publish"). Everything else is **engine** work.

- **Do not stage the content surface** in a feature commit. Dirty content files sitting next to your work are not yours to commit — leave them.
- Commit engine work with `bun run commit:engine "message" <paths you changed>`. It refuses content paths and reports what it held back. **Always pass your paths** — the no-paths form sweeps every dirty engine file in the tree, including work from other sessions, and warns you when it does.
- Only exception: a schema migration that forces content JSON to change alongside the code. Commit them together and say so in the message.

See CLAUDE.md → *Content vs engine*.

## PRs and main

- **Open PR** ≠ merge. Merge only when the user asks.
- After merge, switch to `main` (`git checkout main && git pull`), then reload the browser. Production deploys from `main` push (Cloudflare Pages).
- **After every merge — delete the feature branch (do this from `main`):** remove the **remote** branch (`git push origin --delete <branch>` or `gh pr merge --delete-branch`) and the **local** branch (`git branch -d <branch>`). Do not leave merged branches around to pile up. Skip only for stacked PRs still based on that branch. See Atlas `standards.md` → *Git — Delete merged feature branches*.
- **After merge or an impactful commit:** always log a short **why / learning / reuse** note to Atlas (`learnings.md`, `decisions-log.md`, or `standards.md`) in the same turn — do not wait to be asked. Skip only if nothing new. See Atlas `standards.md` → *Git — Log learnings after merge / impactful commit*.

## Dev session

Reuse the existing dev session (`bun run dev:session:status`) — do not start duplicate servers. See `dev-session.mdc`.
